{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3411","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3411","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3411\",\"parent_revision\":\"abac92ccd47b578755f1dcb89329edf41d789cb2ab011e858ffabe6d2b3fb83c\",\"root_revision\":\"abac92ccd47b578755f1dcb89329edf41d789cb2ab011e858ffabe6d2b3fb83c\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-09-04\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`sam_schema/backlog.py`'s CLI `add` command now exits non-zero whenever `result[\\\"error\\\"]` is set \u2014 including the tolerated \\\"item stored, GitHub issue creation failed\\\" case, not just genuine total failure. `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/quick/start.md`'s `backlog add` invocation has no accompanying guidance for this, unlike `create/start.md` which #3182 updated with an explicit branch (item stored, use `reference`, don't treat as fatal).\\n\\nAn agent following `quick/start.md` literally after this partial-failure case has no instruction to inspect the JSON body before treating the non-zero exit as fatal \u2014 risking either a spurious retry (creating a duplicate local item) or silently swallowing a real, actionable failure reason.\\n\\nSame pattern/scope as followup #3400 (`interop/SKILL.md`'s identical gap for the MCP path), discovered by an independent code-review pass on PR #3404 rather than the original grooming/architecture Impact Radius, which only found `create/start.md` as a consumer.\\n\\nUser-provided context: likely the same fix shape as `create/start.md` Step 5's branch \u2014 check for a populated `error` alongside a stored item (non-empty `item_ref`/`reference`), report it, and continue rather than treating the exit code alone as fatal. Exact wording is design work for grooming.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Code review on PR #3404 (backlog_add silent-failure fix, #3182)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-04\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"3aa85ac921829e641fb041095985ab9c3f86cf6ddb0af6f48e08ce883d30d549\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABStoi_g\"}"}